    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my bamboo palm leaf tips turning brown?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Brown tips on bamboo palm fronds usually come from one of three causes: air that is too dry for the plant, salts from tap water or fertiliser building up in the mix, or uneven watering. Bamboo palm has a poor tolerance of salts, so salt build-up is a common cause in the UAE."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my bamboo palm leaves turning yellow?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yellow or brown fronds low on a bamboo palm are usually normal ageing: older fronds die off as new canes grow. Yellowing across the whole plant, with mix that stays wet, points to overwatering and root problems. Too little light can also turn the fronds yellow."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why are my bamboo palm canes going soft or collapsing?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Soft, dark canes, a smell from the pot or a dying centre on a bamboo palm mean rot. Waterlogged, overwatered mix causes root rot, stem rot and bud rot in bamboo palms."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What are the fine webs and pale speckles on my bamboo palm?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Fine webbing and pale, speckled fronds on a bamboo palm are signs of spider mites. UF/IFAS notes that spider mites and scale can become serious pests of bamboo palms grown indoors."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What are the white cotton patches or brown bumps on my bamboo palm?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "White, cottony patches on a bamboo palm are mealybugs, and small brown or grey bumps that scrape off are scale insects. Both suck sap and are common indoor pests of bamboo palms."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What are the reddish-brown dead patches on my bamboo palm?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Reddish-brown dead areas on bamboo palm fronds are typical of cold damage. Penn State Extension says this usually happens at about 7 °C or below; cold draughts from AC vents, windows and doors also damage fronds."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Why does my bamboo palm have pale or scorched patches?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Pale, bleached or brown dry patches on a bamboo palm are usually sun scorch. In the UAE this often happens behind west- or south-facing glass, or outdoors without full shade."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Is a bamboo palm the same as a parlour palm?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A bamboo palm and a parlour palm are not quite the same. The bamboo palm is Chamaedorea seifrizii, a taller, clumping palm with cane-like stems. The parlour palm, Chamaedorea elegans, is a smaller relative that is also sold as bamboo palm. Their care is almost the same."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can a bamboo palm live outside in the UAE?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A bamboo palm can live outside in the UAE only in full shade with shelter from wind, and best in the cooler months from October to April. In summer, daytime heat around 41–42 °C and warm nights are hard on a shade palm, so most do better indoors. Inland and in colder GCC cities, bring it in on winter nights below about 7 °C."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does a bamboo palm clean the air?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A bamboo palm does not noticeably clean the air in a normal room. Studies that found potted plants removing chemicals were done in small sealed chambers, and a 2019 review found that a building would need 10 to 1,000 plants per square metre of floor to match normal ventilation. Choose a bamboo palm for its looks and easy care."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can a bamboo palm live indoors under AC all year?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, a bamboo palm can live indoors under AC all year. Air-conditioned UAE homes and offices sit close to the 21–27 °C that Penn State Extension gives as ideal for indoor palms. Keep the bamboo palm out of direct sun and out of the direct flow of the AC vent, and test the mix before you water."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Can a bamboo palm grow in low light?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, a bamboo palm tolerates low light, and NC State Extension calls it an excellent houseplant for low-light areas. It grows more slowly in a dim spot, so give it medium or bright indirect light for the fullest growth."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How tall does a bamboo palm grow?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "NC State Extension gives a bamboo palm a height of about 0.9–2.3 m, and Penn State Extension says it reaches about 2 m. Outdoors in tropical gardens it can grow taller. New canes keep growing from the base, so the clump also gets wider."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How fast does a bamboo palm grow?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A bamboo palm grows slowly to moderately. New canes grow from the base, so the palm fills out over time more than it shoots up. Low light and winter slow it down."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Does a bamboo palm flower?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A bamboo palm flowers sometimes. It can produce small pale-yellow flowers on stalks that turn orange, followed by small black fruit. Male and female flowers grow on separate plants, so fruit forms only when both are present. The fruit juice can irritate sensitive skin."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How is plant size measured?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Size is measured from the bottom of the nursery pot to the top tip of the highest leaf. A plant listed as 50-60 CM stands in that range measured this way."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Which pot option should I choose, nursery or decorative?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Choose the nursery pot for the lowest price or if you already have a planter. Choose a decorative pot for a ready-to-display plant that arrives fully potted with soil mix, perlite and a drainage layer. The plant itself is the same."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Do the decorative pots have drainage holes?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Decorative pot orders include a drainage layer at the base, with premium soil mix and perlite. For specific details on a particular pot model, send us the product link and our team will confirm."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Is the plant healthy on arrival? Can I check first?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Plants are guaranteed to arrive healthy. Check your plant with the delivery agent: if it's damaged or not what you ordered, you can refuse it on the spot. If you find damage after unpacking, send photos and your order number on WhatsApp (+971 4 294 1422) or email sales@plantsworld.ae within 24 hours and we'll replace it free. You can also ask for a pre-dispatch photo."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "My plant arrived with a few drooping or yellow leaves. Is that normal?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes, that's normal. A few drooping, bent or yellow leaves are a common reaction to the journey and a new spot, and plants usually recover within a few days. Keep it in bright indirect light and check the soil before watering. If the plant or pot is actually damaged, send photos within 24 hours."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Will my plant be safe in the UAE heat during delivery?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. Our own delivery team brings your order, not a third-party courier. In extreme summer heat (June to September) we may move deliveries to farther emirates to a cooler day and agree the new day with you. If anything arrives damaged, we replace it free."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Will my plant look exactly like the website photo?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "You'll receive the variety and size you ordered, but every plant grows individually, so leaf count, shape and shade can differ from the photo, which is representative. For peace of mind, ask for a pre-dispatch photo at checkout or on WhatsApp."
     }
    }
